<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duarte Barbosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duarte Barbosa was a Portuguese writer and official who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> as a scribe and interpreter from around 1500. His Book of Duarte Barbosa, completed about 1516, is one of the earliest European accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> world, describing the towns of the East African coast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, India and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. He was killed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1521 during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a>'s voyage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duarte-barbosa.jpg" alt="Duarte Barbosa" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Edward John Stanley, Baron Stanley, 1827-1903 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Voyage_Round_The_World_Signatures_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
